cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Please cite this project and the upstream manuscript. This is a conditional
  research draft; include the repository commit used until a release is archived.
  On the community integration branch also credit the imported contributors
  identified in CONTRIBUTORS.md, NOTICE and the source-specific manifests.
title: "A sharper exponent for integer multiplication"
authors:
  - family-names: Colkitt
    given-names: Douglas
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds"
url: "https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds"
abstract: >-
  A conditional integer-multiplication checkpoint with kappa = 2^-30,
  using a ternary five-subset network, rational address frames, compact
  controls and the retained compressed complex network. Includes exact
  certificates, a proof note and an independent manuscript patch. The
  upstream theorem and identified extensions remain assumptions. Earlier
  related ternary work by Zhihao Chen in PR #7 is acknowledged; this
  checkpoint makes no priority or strongest-known-bound claim.
keywords:
  - integer multiplication
  - computational complexity
  - exact arithmetic
  - parameter optimization
  - reproducible research
references:
  - type: unpublished
    title: "Integer multiplication below n log n"
    authors:
      - name: OpenAI
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/openai/math/tree/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Integer-multiplication-below-n-log-n-September-23-2026"
